
================================================================
 ZYNQ-7000 SECURITY POSTURE   (UG585 v1.12.2 Appendix B)
 mem-AP: uscale.axi
================================================================
 devcfg: CTRL=0x0c00607f LOCK=0x00000000 STATUS=0x40000820 MCTRL=0x1c000000
----------------------------------------------------------------
 (1) IDENTITY
   PSS_IDCODE               Zynq-7000  device=7z020 (code 0x07)  IDCODE rev=1
   Silicon version (PS_VERSION) 2.0 (code 1)
 (2) BOOT
   Boot device (BOOT_MODE)  Quad-SPI (0x1); PLL enabled; JTAG chain cascade
   Last reset cause         POR
   BootROM error code       0x0000 (clean boot)
 (3) SECURE BOOT & eFUSE
   Booted securely (SEC_EN) no — non-secure boot (dev/default)
   eFuse SECURE_EN          not blown — non-secure boot permitted (dev)
   eFuse JTAG_DIS           not blown — JTAG/DAP allowed
   eFuse SW_RESERVE         not blown — BBRAM key usable
   Secure lockdown          clear
   DEVCI illegal-access     clear
 (4) DEBUG / DAP
   ARM DAP (DAP_EN)         ENABLED (111)
   Invasive (DBGEN)         enabled
   Non-invasive (NIDEN)     enabled
   Secure-inv (SPIDEN)      enabled
   Secure-non-inv (SPNIDEN) enabled
   JTAG scan chain          enabled
   Debug lock (LOCK.DBG)    open — debug enables WRITABLE (reopen possible)
 (5) CRYPTO
   PL AES engine (AES_EN)   off (000 / dev)
   AES key source (FUSE)    BBRAM key
   SEU lockdown (SEU_EN)    off
 (6) CONFIG LOCK & TRUSTZONE
   SLCR write-protect       unlocked (sys-ctrl regs writable)
   APU CFGSDISABLE          clear
   APU CP15SDISABLE         clear
   DMAC TrustZone (TZ_DMA_NS) secure
   DMAC peripheral TZ       TZ_DMA_PERIPH_NS = 0x0 (per-channel NS bits)
----------------------------------------------------------------
 VERDICT: ALL-OPEN dev baseline — DAP+debug on, non-secure boot, no eFuse hardening
